2. Platform Model

2.1 Feed Architecture [Primary]

X's For You feed operates as a multi-stage pipeline. Candidate retrieval draws from three systems: Thunder (in-network, followed accounts), Phoenix retrieval (out-of-network, vector similarity), and SimClusters (out-of-network, community detection via matrix factorization anchoring users and posts into approximately 145,000 community vectors). The configuration parameters confirm that all three sources are enabled by default: EnablePhoenixSource (default true), EnableSimclustersSource (default true), and ThunderMaxResults (default 1200 candidates).

Ranking is performed by Phoenix, a Grok-derived transformer trained on xAI's Grok-1 architecture. Phoenix reads the viewer's recent action history and predicts the probability of each engagement action per candidate. The final score is Σ weight × predicted probability. X's own README explicitly warns: "The weights scale the predicted probabilities of such actions... they do not scale the raw engagement counts, so e.g. it'd be incorrect to see that a report has 468 times higher weight than a like and conclude that e.g. '1 report cancels out 468 likes.'"

