3. Strategic Implementation

Vector Implementation
Replies / quotes (5) Close every post with an exact, answerable technical question or falsification condition, not a rhetorical one.
Copy-link and DM shares (20 / 5) [Inference] Build "send this to a colleague" artifacts: definitions, one-page maps, proof sketches, checklists. Reference-grade material is what copy-link shares reward.
Follows (4) Make the profile and pinned post legible as a research program: seven domains, repo link, version.
Topical identity [Inference] Keep vocabulary consistent within a domain per post; avoid mixing all seven domains in one week's feed.
Mutual-follow replies (+15 boost) Engage genuinely and repeatedly with a small set of peers who also follow back. No follow-for-follow.
Author diversity [Inference] Do not release multiple major items within the same few hours. A 10-post thread may compete with itself; A/B test thread vs. single long-form vs. Article.
Links Default: self-contained main post, source link in the final post of a thread or as a first reply. Because replies get weaker out-of-network distribution, test putting the DOI/repo in the main post. Choose by measured outcome.
Negative feedback Overclaiming, bait, or hype risks mute/not-interested/report — the heaviest coefficients. The Adversarial Gate is also a distribution safeguard.
30-minute loop Editorial discipline, kept. [Unsupported] as an algorithm claim.

3.1 Formats Available [Secondary]

Standard posts, 25,000-character long-form posts (Premium), and Articles (~100,000 characters, any Premium tier since January 2026). Articles are treated similarly to external links by the ranking system: the algorithm does not reward the Article post itself with wide organic distribution; engagement on the preview post drives distribution.

Format experiment: For the first six releases, alternate thread / long-form post / Article for comparable material, and compare Qualified Peer Engagements per impression.

3.2 LaTeX Rendering

Native LaTeX rendering on X is [Unsupported]. The browser extension Marked'X-Down provides offline KaTeX rendering for inline ($...$) and display ($$...$$) formulas, activated by including the hashtag #latexed or #LaTeXed in the post. Default to image-rendered equations or Unicode.

3.3 Cadence Cap [Inference]

At most one major item per day, to respect author diversity decay.

