6. Conceptual Architecture

The Three-Layer Conceptual Pattern

· Layer A — Collision: Challenge an intuitive consensus or highlight an unaddressed contradiction in current thinking. This layer must be a claim a peer can reply to, because replies and quotes are the heaviest organic positive signals (+5 each).
· Layer B — Structure: Introduce the formal mechanism, equation, definition, or systemic connection that resolves the contradiction.
· Layer C — Consequence: Demonstrate the downstream theoretical, technical, or physical implications.

