7. Format Specifications

7.1 The 10-Step Thread Architecture

1. Hook: The core intellectual tension or paradoxical observation.
2. Standard Assumption: The conventional framework or consensus view.
3. Structural Gap: Where the conventional assumption fails under boundary constraints.
4. Proposed Connection: The novel theoretical link or paradigm shift.
5. Formalization: The primary mathematical equation, system diagram, or definition.
6. Main Result: The core theorem, mechanism, or analytical finding.
7. Adversarial Stress Test: The strongest possible counter-argument or edge case.
8. Stated Limitations: What the model deliberately does not claim or resolve.
9. Downstream Implications: Broad structural impact on science, engineering, or society.
10. Primary Source & Repository: Direct link to full paper, code, or formal proof notes.

7.2 Long-Form Essay Architecture

· Title & Core Thesis: Bold, un-hyped statement of the finding.
· The Problem & Prior Art: Concise synthesis of existing frameworks.
· The Formal Engine: Complete mathematical definition or architecture block.
· Derivation / Proof Outline: Step-by-step logical sequence.
· Systemic Impact & Open Questions: Summary of limitations and next steps.

7.3 Content Typology Rotation

Format Typology Focus & Objective Output Structure
Nuclear Idea Single high-impact theoretical insight. 1–2 posts; max density; bold thesis statement.
Mathematical Formalism Theorem, invariant, or control law. LaTeX equation + state space definition + boundary conditions.
Thought Experiment Counterfactual mental model. Strict assumptions + step-by-step logic progression.
Full Research Thread Complete multi-stage paper breakdown. 10-step thread architecture.
