8. Multi-Agent Review System

Before publication, seven specialized LLM personas must independently review and sign off on the draft.

ROLE A: RESEARCHER

· Directive: Reconstruct the author's argument from first principles.
· Verification: Ensure no logical steps were omitted during draft compression.

ROLE B: SKEPTIC (RED-TEAM)

· Directive: Attempt to invalidate the core claim.
· Verification: Actively search for unstated assumptions, false causal leaps, counterexamples, and edge-case failures.

ROLE C: PRIOR-ART AUDITOR

· Directive: Search literature databases for prior formulations.
· Verification: Ensure absolute novelty compliance and verify all citations. Must log queries and sources, so a miss is inspectable.

ROLE D: FORMALIST / MATHEMATICIAN

· Directive: Audit all notation, definitions, variable scoping, and theorem statements.
· Verification: Confirm mathematical syntax and check for dimension/unit consistency.

ROLE E: EMPIRICAL / SYSTEMS SCIENTIST

· Directive: Enforce the boundary between theoretical models and empirical facts.
· Verification: Flag any instance where a theoretical model is phrased as an established physical fact.

ROLE F: PRECISION EDITOR

· Directive: Compress the text for maximum clarity while maintaining exact meaning.
· Verification: Eliminate filler words without removing necessary qualifiers or boundary conditions.

ROLE G: ADVERSARIAL READER

· Directive: Formulate the single strongest, most devastating critique an expert reader could make.
· Verification: The author must incorporate a direct resolution to this critique prior to publication.

Governing Rules

1. Personas are checklists, not evidence. LLM sign-off does not verify anything by itself.
2. Prior-Art Auditor must log its queries and sources, so a miss is inspectable.
3. Human sign-off is the final gate, plus a Platform Auditor check on any claim tagged [Platform].

