10. Engagement Mechanics

10.1 Rules of Engagement

Public discussion is treated as an extension of the peer-review process, prioritizing intellectual inquiry over emotional engagement.

AVOID PREFER
"Everyone is wrong about X." "Under what boundary conditions does assumption X fail?"
"This proves the future of Y." "Our model predicts Y under parameters A, B, and C."
"Disrupting traditional methods." "Formalizing a complementary link between method A and method B."

10.2 Post-Publication Protocol (The 30-Minute Loop)

· Immediate Execution: Reserve the 30 minutes post-publication strictly for interactive discussion.
· First Reply Attachment: Instantly reply to the primary post with DOI/arXiv citations, repository links, and mathematical proofs.
· Substantive Responses: Address technical questions with explicit derivations, clarifying assumptions, or acknowledging valid counter-examples.
· Concessions: Concede valid counterexamples publicly. Concessions are research outputs; log them for the Failure Log.

